               "caution":  "Sharp single-day rallies inside a deep downtrend often fail at overhead resistance unless followed by sustained volume and higher lows. Beyond chart risk, Navitas still generates only $14–$16 million per quarter while guiding Q4 non-GAAP operating expenses to $24–$26 million, meaning meaningful cash burn continues. Meanwhile, share count has swelled to 261.5 million, valuation remains rich relative to current sales, and aggressive GaN launches from rivals like Renesas could squeeze margins before 800V AI rack adoption scales into volume production.",
