               "fundamental":  "Navitas designs gallium-nitride (GaN) and silicon-carbide power chips aimed at replacing legacy silicon inside 800-volt DC AI server racks. Its Nov 3, 2026 Q3 report showed the \"Navitas 2.0\" pivot gaining traction: revenue reached $14.0 million (+33% QoQ, +38% YoY—its first annual growth since 2024), while non-GAAP gross margin improved to 40.0% and GAAP gross margin reached 21.5%. Management guided Q4 revenue to $15.5–$16.5 million (+119% YoY at the midpoint). Strategically, closing the up-to-$232.8 million Claros buyout on Oct 6 adds integrated voltage regulators, complementing NVIDIA 800V-to-12V board work and US-fabbed Gen 5 GaN from GlobalFoundries. However, Q3 GAAP net loss widened to $37.1 million (non-GAAP loss $6.9 million), and Q4 non-GAAP OpEx of $24–$26 million shows profitability remains distant despite roughly $405 million in post-deal debt-free cash.",
