               "opportunity":  "For long-term AI-infrastructure investors, Navitas offers pure-play exposure to the shift from legacy 48V/54V power shelves toward megawatt-scale 800V DC racks. Collaborating with NVIDIA on 800V-to-12V boards, partnering with Microchip on 800V reference designs, and adding Claros\u0027s integrated voltage regulators gives Navitas a broader grid-to-processor footprint. With roughly $405 million in debt-free cash after the Claros closing and US-based Gen 5 GaN production ramping at GlobalFoundries, the company has multi-year runway to convert design wins into volume revenue.",
               "opportunityCheck":  "The page\u0027s AI-opportunity profile is broadly sensible, though AI revenue exposure warrants a modest upward adjustment. Navitas is actively exiting low-end mobile chargers, and high-power AI data-center and grid sales grew over 50% sequentially in Q3 2026, heading past 40% of revenue by year-end. Conversely, market position and bottleneck pricing power should stay restrained: while the NVIDIA 800V board and Claros voltage-regulator buyout strengthen optionality, Navitas\u0027s second patent suit against Renesas proves larger rivals are encroaching on data-center GaN, limiting near-term pricing power.",
