               "summary":  "Navitas Semiconductor (NVTS) jumped 20.56% to $7.33 on Nov 23, 2026, rebounding from its $6.03 52-week low amid a broad AI-chip rally rather than fresh company news. Technically, the stock remains in a steep downtrend—78.5% below its $34.17 high and well under all key moving averages. Fundamentally, Q3 2026 results on Nov 3 showed a real pivot: revenue rose 38% year-over-year to $14.0 million as AI data-center demand accelerated. Still, a $37.1 million GAAP net loss, rising expenses, and a new patent battle with Renesas keep the long-term moat under watch.",
               "technical":  "Despite surging 20.56% to $7.33 on Nov 23, 2026, NVTS remains in a confirmed bearish trend. The stock trades far beneath its exponential moving averages (EMAs, which smooth trend direction): EMA 50 sits at $9.60, EMA 100 at $11.10, and EMA 200 at $11.66, stacked in bearish order with shorter averages below longer ones. Momentum is still negative. MACD (a trend-momentum gauge comparing two moving averages) reads -0.72 below its -0.57 signal line, keeping the histogram negative at -0.15. RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge where under 30 is oversold) bounced to 41.75—no longer oversold, yet still below the 50 midpoint. Within Bollinger Bands (a 20-day volatility channel), price rebounded off the $6.44 lower band but remains beneath the $8.48 middle band and $10.52 upper band, sitting just above its $6.03 52-week low and 78.5% under its $34.17 high. Volume reached 17.30 million shares versus the 14.82 million 20-day average—modestly elevated relief buying, not a breakout. Key support lies at $6.44 and $6.03; overhead resistance stands at $8.48 and $9.60."
